decision: changes-requested

Four defects remain open. Findings are based on code inspection; sandbox restrictions prevented new builds or fixture tests. The sealed integration test passes but does not cover these cases.

Git’s [graph loader](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/master/commit-graph.c) confirms that it prefers a monolithic graph and searches alternate object directories, including for split-chain layers.

Rules applied: backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence. The change follows D1’s proportionate design: explicit maintenance through doctor, with no governance-read writes. CI placement and the report format are compatible.

The surface-check rerun passed. The artifact-check rerun selected a later origin revision; I used the supplied sealed-range output for attribution. Validation relies on sealed evidence. No files were changed or attestation recorded.

In the draft, `finding` means the criterion failed; all findings are blockers.

